I will examine both documents **provision by provision and amendment by amendment**, not merely rely on isolated wording.

For each issue, I will consider:

- the law before and after the amendment;
- the Finance Act or notification through which the change was introduced;
- the applicable tax year and effective date;
- interaction with definitions, schedules, withholding provisions, exemptions, minimum tax and procedural sections;
- corresponding Income Tax Rules, prescribed forms and IRIS requirements;
- transitional, saving and retrospective-effect issues;
- FBR’s likely administrative interpretation;
- exposure during audit, amendment proceedings, recovery and appeal;
- practical tax planning and documentary requirements.

The Income Tax Ordinance supplied is stated to be amended up to **30 June 2026**, so it will generally be the primary current statutory reference. fileciteturn0file1 The uploaded Income Tax Rules are amended only up to **24 November 2023**; therefore, where a post-2023 amendment, SRO, notification or revised procedure may affect the Rules, I will specifically identify that limitation and verify the subsequent legal position instead of assuming the older Rules remain fully current. fileciteturn0file0

I will also distinguish carefully between:

**Substantive liability** — whether income is taxable, exempt, adjustable, minimum or final tax.

**Computation** — admissible expenses, depreciation, losses, credits and applicable rates.

**Withholding treatment** — deduction or collection rate, filer status, adjustable/minimum/final character and reporting responsibility.

**Procedure** — return filing, wealth reconciliation, notices, audit, assessment, appeal, stay and recovery.

**Practical position** — how the provision is actually applied through IRIS and handled before Inland Revenue authorities.

These are very lengthy statutes, so I will not represent that every amendment has already been fully analysed merely by opening the files. I will maintain this detailed contextual approach throughout our discussion and conduct focused full-document review whenever you raise a section, transaction, tax year or client situation.
